This directory contains tests to be run with clang's libFuzzer. See qtbase/tests/libfuzzer/README
for general info about this approach.

In the case of PDFium fuzzing: PDFium's own allocation-size sanity check (FX_OutOfMemoryTerminate)
can deliberately abort() on a single input that computes an absurd allocation size (e.g. a corrupt
object/page count) -- that's intentional hardening, not a bug, and matches how PDFium's own upstream
fuzzing treats this crash class.

Run the fuzzer like this to keep going if it crashes, and to use the AFL dictionary:

$ cd pdf/qpdfdocument/load
<build it>
$ ./load -fork=1 -ignore_crashes=1 -ignore_ooms=1 -ignore_timeouts=1 -dict=path/to/afl-x.xxx/dictionaries/pdf.dict

PDFium already gets fuzzing upstream; see
qtwebengine/src/3rdparty/chromium/third_party/pdfium/testing/fuzzers
